table_structure.prompt:
You are given the words of one PDF page, each with an id, its text and its box. Find the table(s) among them and return their STRUCTURE only: JSON {"tables": [{"rows": [[["<word id>", ...], ...], ...]}]}. Each row is a list of cells top to bottom; each cell is a list of word ids left to right, or {"words": [...], "colspan": n, "rowspan": n} for a spanning cell; an empty cell is []. Use every word inside a table exactly once and never write any text yourself: only ids from the list. Words outside tables are not part of the answer.

Words:
{words_json}
